{"study_accession":"PRJNA544334","secondary_study_accession":"SRP201203","title":"Human CD90+CD34+ cells are phenotypically, transcriptionally and functionally the most refined target for hematopoietic stem cell gene therapy","description":"Hematopoietic stem cell (HSC) gene therapy and editing has the potential to treat and even cure many genetic diseases and cancer. The ability to target gene modification to a more refined HSC-enriched population would improve efficiency and feasibility while potentially decreasing off target effects. We recently described the CD34+CD90+CD45RA- cell fraction as such an enriched HSC population in nonhuman primates (NHPs). We showed that CD34+CD90+CD45RA– cells were exclusively responsible for rapid and robust multilineage engraftment in NHPs. Here we studied human HSC-enriched cell populations combining cell surface markers, high-throughput single cell RNA sequencing (scRNAseq), and functional mouse engraftment studies. We found that only human CD34+CD90+CD45RA– cells were capable of multilineage engraftment and at the same time complete repopulation of the bone marrow stem cell compartment. Combining phenotypical and scRNAseq analysis, we further found that CD34+CD90+CD45RA– cells were nearly entirely depleted of lineage-committed progenitor cells and markedly enriched for transcriptionally most primitive progenitor cells. Most important for clinical applications, CD34+CD90+CD45RA– cells demonstrated the most efficient reduction of target cells compared to CD34+CD38low/– or CD34+CD133+ cells. These studies support the use of CD34+CD90+CD45RA– cells as target cell population for HSC gene therapy and editing approaches in humans.","pubmed":"","geo_series":"","n_samples":20,"samples":[{"sample_accession":"SAMN11851211","study_accession":"PRJNA544334","blood_class":"bone_marrow","class_from":"sample","title":"Human sample from Homo sapiens","description":"Enriched for Hematopoietic Stem Cells (HSC)","sex":"not provided","geo_sample":"","access":"open","dbgap":"","n_runs":1,"first_public":"2020-06-02","attributes":[["isolate","Bone marrow aspirate"],["age","not collected"],["biomaterial_provider","Co-operative Center for Excellence in Hematology (CCEH), Fred Hutchinson Cancer Research Center, Seattle, WA, 98109"],["sex","not provided"],["tissue","Steady state bone marrow"],["cell_type","Hematopoietic stem and progenitor cells"],["dev_stage","adult"],["disease","healthy"],["phenotype","CD34+CD133+CD45RA-CD90+"],["class","2327_CD90P"]],"runs":[{"run_accession":"SRR9282987","experiment_accession":"SRX6052711","library_layout":"PAIRED","library_selection":"Oligo-dT","instrument_model":"Illumina HiSeq 2500","read_count":27193630,"base_count":2719363000,"first_public":"2020-06-02","experiment_title":"Illumina HiSeq 2500 sequencing: RNA-Seq of humans: Bone marrow CD34+CD90+ HSPCs"}],"labels":[]},{"sample_accession":"SAMN11851212","study_accession":"PRJNA544334","blood_class":"bone_marrow","class_from":"sample","title":"Human sample from Homo sapiens","description":"Enriched for Hematopoietic Stem Cells (HSC)","sex":"not provided","geo_sample":"","access":"open","dbgap":"","n_runs":1,"first_public":"2020-06-02","attributes":[["isolate","Bone marrow aspirate"],["age","not collected"],["biomaterial_provider","Co-operative Center for Excellence in Hematology (CCEH), Fred Hutchinson Cancer Research Center, Seattle, WA, 98109"],["sex","not provided"],["tissue","Steady state bone marrow"],["cell_type","Hematopoietic stem and progenitor cells"],["dev_stage","adult"],["disease","healthy"],["phenotype","CD34+CD133+CD45RA-CD90+"],["class","2417_CD90P"]],"runs":[{"run_accession":"SRR9282988","experiment_accession":"SRX6052710","library_layout":"PAIRED","library_selection":"Oligo-dT","instrument_model":"Illumina HiSeq 2500","read_count":22914250,"base_count":2291425000,"first_public":"2020-06-02","experiment_title":"Illumina HiSeq 2500 sequencing: RNA-Seq of humans: Bone marrow CD34+CD90+ HSPCs"}],"labels":[]},{"sam